    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0615" n="525" xml:id="pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2719b</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-09T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9,
                                1918, 6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>253. The American Ambassador at Tokyo has been ordered to proceed informally to
                    Vladivostok and report to the Department his views as to how the purpose of the
                    United States to assist Russia may be furthered under the conditions which he
                    will find to exist there. His reports will be for the special information of the
                    Department and his stay at Vladivostok will be unofficial and temporary.</p>
                <p>The following supplementary instructions have been sent him today: [Here follows
                    telegram to the Ambassador in Japan, dated September 9, 1918, 5 p.m., <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg372">page 372</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
